      <text bytes="635" sha1="auc52oi3ko9t0kowsxkp0ucp9nubtx4" xml:space="preserve">Are most of the people posting now just finding out about this?



literally stumped, but I have some therory to spout.



First off, I am nowhere near intellegent by my standards, just know, this is all uninformed rambling.

a quote on the fibbonacci page is "This grows according to the rules that every mature branch sprouts a new branch at the end of each year, and new branches take a year to reach maturity."

Of course this makes me thing of the anual puzzles, but also that buddist cycle of death and rebirth (which without finding out about that I wouldn't be here at all)



maybe this puzzle has to do with the cycle of life</text>
